&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring an Associate, Insurance Product &amp;amp; Emerging Solutions to join our Insurance Product Development team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate, Insurance Product &amp;amp; Emerging Solutions supports the development, execution, and optimization of innovative health solutions across Oscar’s Individual and Family Plan (IFP) product portfolio. This role partners cross-functionally to support product strategy, market research, member engagement initiatives, and lifecycle management activities that improve member experience, affordability, retention, and long-term product performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate supports the translation of enterprise and market priorities into actionable product initiatives through structured analysis, operational coordination, and disciplined execution across market leadership, actuarial, compliance, product management, compliance, regulatory, and operational teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Vice President, Insurance Product Innovation and Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This is a remote / work-from-home role. You must reside in one of the following states: Arizona, California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Massachusetts, Michigan, Nevada, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Texas, or Virginia. Note, this list of states is subject to change. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $106,812 - $140,190 per year in New Jersey, New York, and California. The base pay for all other locations is: $96,130 - $126,171 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Strategy &amp;amp; Innovation Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and execution of product and innovation initiatives across Oscar’s product portfolio and emerging solution domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and translate market research, competitive data sets, and performance assessments to support product strategy recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in identifying growth opportunities, including lifestyle-oriented products, population specific solutions, and adjacent offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development of business cases, market insights, and product recommendations in partnership with actuarial, finance, market leadership, and marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze member, market, and performance data to identify trends, risks, and optimization opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Design, Integration, and Lifecycle Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ongoing product lifecycle activities, including launch readiness, post-launch monitoring, optimization efforts, and remediation tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with development of product artifacts and documentation required for filings, governance reviews, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional inputs across product, regulatory, actuarial, compliance, operational, and growth teams to support alignment and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support modular product design and portfolio consistency efforts across markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track timelines, dependencies, risks, and deliverables across concurrent work streams and product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in documenting assumptions, decisions, and key learnings to support future planning and audibility of product portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Execution &amp;amp; Operational Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
