&lt;p&gt;Oscar is seeking a Director, Strategic Planning, Office of CEO to help support the development and execution of the company&#39;s strategy. Sitting within Corporate Strategy, this leader will partner across the CEO office, executive leadership, Finance, Communications, People, and business teams to connect enterprise priorities with leadership decision-making and accountable execution. This role requires a strong strategy operator who can synthesize complex issues, create executive-ready narratives, and build the planning architecture that helps Oscar scale with clarity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Vice President, Corporate Strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our New York, NY office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $ $198,720 - $260,820 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and manage the CEO operating agenda, ensuring executive forums are focused on the highest-value strategic, operational, and organizational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders to translate CEO priorities into clear strategic narratives, decision points, ownership models, and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-ready materials that clarify complex topics, elevate key tradeoffs, and support high-quality leadership decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases that quantify opportunities, surface investment needs, clarify tradeoffs, and support executive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visibility across critical company priorities and identify where additional structure, escalation, or executive alignment is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted &lt;em&gt;strategy&lt;/em&gt; partner to Corporate Strategy leadership and the CEO office on emerging priorities, special projects, and enterprise planning moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help strengthen Oscar&#39;s operating rhythm as the company scales, with a focus on clarity, accountability, and disciplined execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in strategy, business operations, corporate planning, chief of staff, or related roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience developing executive presentations, board materials, strategic recommendations, or business cases for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience supporting executive leadership, corporate strategy, business operations, or enterprise planning initiatives in a cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing or improving strategic planning processes, operating cadences, governance frameworks, or cross-functional operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience leading complex, cross-functional initiatives involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience partnering with senior executives to drive strategic initiatives, organizational planning, or business transformation efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced, high-growth, or highly regulated organizations where priorities frequently evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or equivalent graduate business training preferred; recent MBA graduates with relevant strategy experience are encouraged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare, insurance, technology, or regulated industry experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity. Learn more about how you can safeguard yourself from recruitment fraud&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://hioscar.com/careers/recruitment-fraud-alert&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
