&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Senior Analyst, Individual and Family Plan Insurance Solutions to join our Insurance Product Development team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Analyst, Individual and Family Plan Insurance Solutions, provides foundational analytical research and product level support across Oscar’s individual and family (IFP) and employer-subsidized product portfolios. This role focuses on data analysis, market and competitive research, and performance monitoring of our markets to inform product strategy, design decisions, and execution readiness across on-exchange and employer-subsidized (ICHRA) solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role operates horizontally across product lines and segments, serving as an insight engine for product teams and enabling data-driven decision making in a regulated, multi-market environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Vice President, Insurance Product Innovation and Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This is a remote / work-from-home role. You must reside in one of the following states: Arizona, California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Massachusetts, Michigan, Nevada, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Texas, or Virginia. Note, this list of states is subject to change. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $83,628 - $109,761 per year in New Jersey, New York, and California. The base pay for all other locations is: $75,265 - $98,785 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market, Policy, and Competitive Research&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Play a key role in building, maintaining and identifying improvements to models that forecast membership growth and retention rates in support of strategic decisions&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Conduct market and competitive research across individual and employer-subsidized health insurance offerings&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze competitor plan designs, benefit structures, pricing approaches, and positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track regulatory and policy developments and support impact assessments for product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support population and employer-segment research initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Performance Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Analyze product performance across growth, retention, utilization, and margin metrics&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain recurring dashboards and performance reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support deep-dive analyses for product reviews, remediation efforts, and future-year planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify trends, anomalies, and emerging risks through data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Filing Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support product teams during filing cycles through data validation, QA, and analytical support&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in preparation of analytical material required for regulatory submissions and internal reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data accuracy and consistency across product artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insight Translation &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Translate complex analyses into clear, structured insights for product and cross-functional partners&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare summaries, exhibits, and briefing materials for product leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support documentation of learnings to inform future product cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years developing and managing commercial insurance products.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
