&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a VP, Marketplace ICHRA General Manager to join our Lucie team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lucie is the first all-in-one storefront designed to give consumers, businesses, and employees total control over their healthcare. We’ve replaced the &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; model with a curated menu of medical, dental, vision, and supplemental products to help individuals build a custom bundle that actually protects their wallets.&amp;nbsp;Lucie Inc. is part of Oscar Health (NYSE: OSCR), a leading healthcare technology company built on a full-stack platform and a relentless focus on member experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The VP, Marketplace ICHRA General Manager is a critical executive leader responsible for running and growing the Individual Coverage Health Reimbursement Arrangement (ICHRA) business for Lucie Health Marketplace. Reporting directly to the President of Lucie, this role maintains full strategic and operational ownership over Lucie’s end-to-end ICHRA business line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a proven executive with deep expertise in ICHRA, health insurance technology, and scaling high-performing commercial and business operations teams. It offers a unique opportunity to lead a growth-focused business unit backed by proven proprietary platform technology. The ideal candidate will have the autonomy to build, scale, and lead a market-defining business line positioned at the critical intersection of individual health marketplaces and employer-sponsored benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This is a remote position, open to candidates who reside in: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, Nevada, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, Wisconsin, or Washington, D.C.. A hybrid work schedule, with 3 days of in-office work per week, may be required depending on your metro area.&amp;nbsp;#LI-Remote&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $240,000 - $315,000 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Business Strategy &amp;amp; GTM Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the commercial design, product positioning, and long-term go-to-market strategy to scale Lucie’s market share in the growing ICHRA landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand Distribution Channels:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify, secure, and manage high-value business development relationships, including third-party administrators, agents/agencies, and employers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align Product with Market Demand:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the strategic bridge between market demand and technical execution, collaborating with Product and Engineering leaders to build a scalable, seamless, and best-in-class enrollment experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Commercial Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee B2B marketing initiatives, broker training frameworks, and automated onboarding workflows to drive platform adoption and increase user utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execute Upward Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage financial and operational performance metrics for the business line, regular reporting on progress, and presenting business results to executive leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Manage a High-Performing Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Recruit, mentor, and lead a cross-functional division spanning account management, partnership sales, tech, and business operations specialists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
